Translations, definitions and glosses are derived from the English Wiktionary (https://en.wiktionary.org/), whose text is available under CC BY-SA 4.0 and the GNU Free Documentation License, by Wiktionary contributors. The structured extract was produced by Wiktextract / kaikki.org (Tatu Ylonen, "Wiktextract: Wiktionary as Machine-Readable Structured Data", LREC 2022). Entries marked as machine translations ("src": "ai") were generated by an AI model to fill gaps and are released under the same licence. Word categories are derived from Princeton WordNet 3.0 (WordNet licence, https://wordnet.princeton.edu/license-and-commercial-use). Word frequencies used for selection come from wordfreq (https://github.com/rspeer/wordfreq).

